#!/usr/local/bin/dyalogscript
⍝ Shell against sqlite3 — a SQL database from APL with no driver, no ⎕NA
⍝ and no DLL, because `sqlite3 -batch` is just another line-oriented
⍝ child process (ADR D20; Tutorial step 1b).
⍝
⍝ Nothing here knows about JSON. That's the point: Shell was built for
⍝ NDJSON-framed JSON-RPC, but it has no idea what the lines mean, so any
⍝ interpreter that reads a line and writes lines is a valid peer. Two
⍝ substitutions that behave identically, if you'd rather try them:
⍝
⍝   duckdb -noheader -list        ⍝ same dialect-ish, same line framing
⍝   python -u -i -q               ⍝ then Send 'print(2+2)' and read '4'
⍝
⍝ The -u on Python is not optional: without it Python block-buffers
⍝ stdout as soon as it isn't a terminal, and Receive waits forever for
⍝ output that's sitting in the child's buffer. sqlite3 and duckdb flush
⍝ per statement on their own, which is why they need no such flag.
⍝
⍝ Run: & <dyalog>\scriptbin\dyalogscript.ps1 examples\sqlite-repl.apls
⎕IO←1
⎕FIX'file://D:/devel/mcp-client/src/Shell.dyalog'

⍝ CaptureStderr because sqlite3 reports SQL errors there (see below).
h←(CaptureStderr:1)Shell.Start'sqlite3' '-batch'

⍝ '.mode list' + '.separator |' makes each row exactly one line with a
⍝ known delimiter — i.e. turns sqlite3's output into a framing we can
⍝ actually parse. The default box-drawing table would not be.
h Shell.Send'.mode list'
h Shell.Send'.separator |'
h Shell.Send'create table lang(name text, year integer);'
h Shell.Send'insert into lang values (''APL'',1966),(''SQL'',1974),(''Python'',1991);'

⍝ One Send, three lines back — and nothing in the stream says how many
⍝ to expect. Knowing an answer has ENDED is a protocol problem, not a
⍝ transport one, so we need a convention of our own: a sentinel row.
⍝ (This is exactly the itch JsonRpc's `id` field scratches one layer up.)
∇ rows←h Query sql;line
  h Shell.Send sql
  h Shell.Send'select ''<<end>>'';'
  rows←⍬
  :Repeat
      line←5 Shell.Receive h
      :If line≡'<<end>>' ⋄ :Leave ⋄ :EndIf
      rows,←⊂'|'(≠⊆⊢)line
  :EndRepeat
∇

rows←h Query'select name, year from lang order by year;'
⎕←'rows: ',⍕≢rows
⎕←⍕¨rows

⍝ Ordinary APL on the result, now that it's just nested character data.
⍝ ⎕VFI returns (validMask values) — so the numbers are its SECOND
⍝ element, and ⊃ on the result would quietly hand you the mask instead
⍝ (a bug this example was written with, and caught by the year coming
⍝ out as 1 rather than 1966).
names←⊃¨rows
years←{⊃2⊃⎕VFI 2⊃⍵}¨rows
⎕←'names: ',⍕names
⎕←'oldest: ',(⊃names[⍋years]),' (',(⍕⌊/years),')'

⍝ An aggregate comes back as a single one-row answer, same shape.
⎕←'count/max: ',⍕⊃h Query'select count(*), max(year) from lang;'

⍝ Errors go to STDERR, so the result stream stays clean — which is also
⍝ why a failed query and an empty result are indistinguishable up here
⍝ unless you asked for CaptureStderr.
bad←h Query'select * from no_such_table;'
⎕←'rows from the failed query: ',⍕≢bad
⎕DL 1 ⍝ stdout and stderr are separate streams with no ordering guarantee
⎕←'stderr said: ',⍕h.StderrLines

⍝ ...and the session survives it.
⎕←'still alive: ',⍕⊃h Query'select ''yes'';'

Shell.Stop h
⎕←'status=',h.Status,' killed=',⍕h.Killed
⎕OFF
